For all-even subarrays: y = 0, they're invalid. Count pairs (l, r+1) with P[l] >= P[r+1] and all elements in [l..r] even.

For an all-even subarray, each element adds b, so P[r+1] = P[l] + b*(length) > P[l] (since b >= 1). So P[l] >= P[r+1] never holds for non-empty all-even subarrays! Wait, that means the "y > 0" condition is automatically handled?

