So the answer is simply the number of pairs (i, j) with i < j and P[i] >= P[j].

That's the number of non-strict inversions (count pairs i < j with P[i] >= P[j]).

This can be computed with coordinate compression + BIT (Fenwick tree) in O(n log n).

